Here's the cool thing about being Expert in daggers: The more skilled
you are in daggers, the more of them you get to throw in one turn.  A
character Expert at daggers will throw 2 or 3 of them per attempt.
That's a huge advantage when you have a nice stack of them in your
quiver.  It makes quivered daggers worth far more than wielded
daggers.  It makes wielding daggers long enough to increase your skill
level worth doing, too.

Early on work with the initial long sword long enough to increase its
skill level once.  Then switch to wielding the dagger against the less
impressive monsters long enough to increase its skill level once, but
use "x" to switch to that long sword if you encounter something that is
nasty for your current level.  Keep repeating this cycle until you hit
at least Skilled at both.  Add the war hammer to this cycle until you
get to at least Skilled in it as well.  Then switch to throwing daggers
as their only use.  Or heck, throw daggers as their only use from the
gate but do it a lot.

